{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"wearable-explicable-magpie","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context (discovered while fixing bug 3fa7-94ba-42aa-4623)\n\nThe Gerrit Verified gate executes workflow files from TRUSTED MAIN, not the patchset (proven on change 2115 PS1: its own run 32587991195 still executed main's stale `--timeout=20`, headSha 6a5c88027c5). pytest-timeout precedence is MARKER > CLI > env > INI (`_get_item_settings`, pytest_timeout.py:388; verified empirically incl. marker-applied-at-collection under `-n 2 --dist worksteal`). Consequence: ANY future per-test-budget change carried in `pyproject.toml` is overridden on its own gate run by the previous `--timeout=<old>` CLI flag in `_build-and-test.yml`, so a budget fix can never be exercised by its own Verified run — the class of failure that made 2115 PS1 fail its own gate. Bug 3fa7 was ultimately landed by an operator-cast Verified+1, which is not a repeatable path.\n\n## Proposed mechanism (implemented + validated, preserved on branch `preserve/timeout-floor-hardening` based on a42a9d8d494 — REBASE over 53eaea07aa2 before use)\n\nA conftest FLOOR, not a blanket: `tests/_timeout_floor.py`, called from `tests/conftest.py`'s `pytest_collection_modifyitems` — when the effective non-marker budget (CLI > PYTEST_TIMEOUT env > ini) is positive and BELOW the ini budget, apply the ini budget as `pytest.mark.timeout(budget, method=<ini>, func_only=<ini>)` to every item without an explicit timeout marker. Floor semantics keep the live lanes' deliberately larger CLI budgets (900/600/1800/3600 s) intact (marker > CLI would silently lower them under a blanket), and `--timeout=0` (explicit disable) stays respected. The preserved branch also removes the now-redundant lane flags and rewrites the two parity contracts in tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py accordingly (NOTE: conflicts with 53eaea07aa2's --max-worker-restart=0 lane edit + its parity test; reconcile on rebase).\n\nValidated locally on the preserved branch: a 25 s two-test probe under `-n 2 --dist worksteal --timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread` against the repo config passed with zero node-downs (pre-floor this crashed the workers); a looser CLI budget still wins (floor is not a ceiling); an unmarked over-budget test with no CLI flag is still killed by the ini alone; make lint / typecheck / complexity ratchet green.\n\n## Open design question\n\nFloor semantics neutralize deliberately TIGHTER ad-hoc CLI runs inside tests/ (e.g. crash-amplifier debugging with --timeout=5); such experiments must use a scratch project outside tests/. Decide whether that trade is acceptable, or gate the floor on an env var (e.g. skip when REBAR_TIMEOUT_FLOOR=0).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] An unmarked test whose body fits the ini budget survives a tighter `--timeout` CLI flag; verified by an in-repo contract test with a no-hook negative control.\n- [ ] A larger CLI budget is not lowered by the floor; verified by a contract test.\n- [ ] `--timeout=0` still disables timeouts entirely; verified by a contract test.\n- [ ] Shared-tier lanes' redundant `--timeout`/`--timeout-method` flags removed; parity contracts in test_ci_workflow_parity.py updated without weakening the hang guard (an unmarked hung test is still bounded — negative arm).\n- [ ] docs/local-dev-env.md documents the floor.","id":"5a30-d423-b1f5-4e33","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Make the ini hang budget authoritative over stale trusted-main CLI --timeout flags (conftest marker floor)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787426737780845001,"uuid":"185e62fc-dba2-4f9c-8d77-60ac8bee2612"}